abstract: >-
  A research apparatus for Ignatian spirituality, confined to the old Society
  (1540-1773) and organised in five lines: the founder's own writings (the
  Exercises in a trilingual public-domain parallel edition, the letters of
  1524-1547 in full); the school of discernment (the Official Directory of
  1599, bilingual, and Favre's Memoriale, bilingual); the Society in the
  world; Friedrich Spee; and the counter-voices. With a canonical
  paragraph-level citation index, a cross-corpus concordance, a concept
  atlas, curated reading paths, a discernment lexicon, registers of persons
  and places, and a citation-bound dialogue with the corpus. Four modern
  translations remain in copyright: their structure and anchors are part of
  the apparatus, but no text of them is distributed - a reader opens them
  from a copy they own.
